Subject: dtl: let draws skip a graphics PSO that is still being created

When a draw needs a pipeline the thread pool is still creating,
PipelineState::GetForUse blocks in m_ThreadpoolWork.Wait until the create
finishes. On Windows the driver's compiler is fast and its disk cache
warm, so upstream accepts the wait. Under D3DMetal a first-time pipeline
is a DXIL-to-Metal translation plus a Metal compile. That wait stalls the
batch worker, and once c_MaxOutstandingBatches fill up it stalls the game
thread too, which is the shader-compile stutter D3D11 titles show on this
target.

This adds an opt-in in the style of DXVK_ASYNC. With
CreationArgs::UseNonBlockingPSOs set, PreDraw asks TryGetForUse, which
returns nullptr while the create is still running. PreDraw already turns
a null PSO into a skipped draw, by throwing before either dirty mask is
cleared, so the next draw retries, and the first draw after the create
finishes renders. The cost is the one DXVK_ASYNC has: a one-shot draw
issued while its pipeline compiles is lost.

Only graphics draws skip. PreDispatch, the blit helper and the video
processor still call the blocking GetForUse. A skipped dispatch
(culling, simulation) corrupts later frames rather than one.

PipelineState publishes m_bReady with release after CreateImpl returns
or throws, so a failed create counts as ready and still reaches the
existing null-PSO path. The ImmediateContext counts skipped draws, and
the number and duration of blocking waits, for the D3D11On12 device to
report.

Off by default. A zero-initialized CreationArgs behaves as upstream.
---
diff --git a/include/ImmediateContext.hpp b/include/ImmediateContext.hpp
index e1adad1..747e1f7 100644
--- a/include/ImmediateContext.hpp
+++ b/include/ImmediateContext.hpp
@@ -923,6 +923,7 @@ public:
         UINT DisableGPUTimeout : 1;
         UINT IsXbox : 1;
         UINT AdjustYUY2BlitCoords : 1;
+        UINT UseNonBlockingPSOs : 1;
         GUID CreatorID;
         DWORD MaxAllocatedUploadHeapSpacePerCommandList;
         DWORD MaxSRVHeapSize;
@@ -1596,6 +1597,45 @@ public: // variables
         return m_CreationArgs.UseRoundTripPSOs;
     }
 
+    // Draws skip, rather than wait for, a graphics PSO still being created
+    // on the thread pool. Compute and internal PSOs always wait.
+    bool UseNonBlockingPSOs()
+    {
+        return m_CreationArgs.UseNonBlockingPSOs;
+    }
+
+    struct PipelineCounters
+    {
+        UINT64 DrawsSkippedForPSO;
+        UINT64 PSOWaits;
+        UINT64 PSOWaitNanoseconds;
+    };
+
+    PipelineCounters GetPipelineCounters() const noexcept
+    {
+        PipelineCounters Counters = {};
+        Counters.DrawsSkippedForPSO = m_NumDrawsSkippedForPSO.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        Counters.PSOWaits = m_NumPSOWaits.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        LARGE_INTEGER Frequency;
+        if (QueryPerformanceFrequency(&Frequency) && Frequency.QuadPart > 0)
+        {
+            Counters.PSOWaitNanoseconds = static_cast<UINT64>(
+                static_cast<double>(m_PSOWaitTicks.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) * 1e9
+                / static_cast<double>(Frequency.QuadPart));
+        }
+        return Counters;
+    }
+
+    void RecordPSOWait(INT64 Ticks) noexcept
+    {
+        m_NumPSOWaits.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        m_PSOWaitTicks.fetch_add(static_cast<UINT64>(Ticks), std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
+
+    std::atomic<UINT64> m_NumDrawsSkippedForPSO{ 0 };
+    std::atomic<UINT64> m_NumPSOWaits{ 0 };
+    std::atomic<UINT64> m_PSOWaitTicks{ 0 };
+
     TranslationLayerCallbacks const& GetUpperlayerCallbacks() { return m_callbacks; }
 
     ResidencyManager &GetResidencyManager() { return m_residencyManager; }
diff --git a/include/ImmediateContext.inl b/include/ImmediateContext.inl
index e7be800..609a780 100644
--- a/include/ImmediateContext.inl
+++ b/include/ImmediateContext.inl
@@ -697,9 +697,19 @@ inline void ImmediateContext::PreDraw() noexcept(false)
 
         if (m_StatesToReassert & e_PipelineStateDirty)
         {
-            auto pPSO = m_CurrentState.m_pPSO->GetForUse(COMMAND_LIST_TYPE::GRAPHICS);
+            // Non-blocking: a PSO still compiling skips this draw through the
+            // throw below. Nothing has cleared the dirty bits yet, so the next
+            // draw retries and renders once the PSO is ready.
+            const bool bNonBlocking = UseNonBlockingPSOs();
+            auto pPSO = bNonBlocking
+                ? m_CurrentState.m_pPSO->TryGetForUse(COMMAND_LIST_TYPE::GRAPHICS)
+                : m_CurrentState.m_pPSO->GetForUse(COMMAND_LIST_TYPE::GRAPHICS);
             if (!pPSO)
             {
+                if (bNonBlocking)
+                {
+                    m_NumDrawsSkippedForPSO.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+                }
                 throw RelayHResultError(S_OK);
             }
             GetGraphicsCommandList()->SetPipelineState(pPSO);
diff --git a/include/PipelineState.hpp b/include/PipelineState.hpp
index 0fc6a5b..d8c4c67 100644
--- a/include/PipelineState.hpp
+++ b/include/PipelineState.hpp
@@ -122,11 +122,24 @@ namespace D3D12TranslationLayer
         {
             if (m_ThreadpoolWork)
             {
-                m_ThreadpoolWork.Wait(false);
+                WaitForCreate();
             }
             return DeviceChildImpl::GetForUse(CommandListType);
         }
 
+        // Returns nullptr, without waiting, while the thread-pool create is
+        // still running. Once it has finished this is GetForUse: the Wait
+        // there only reaps the completed work item. A create that failed is
+        // also ready, and returns nullptr from GetForUse as before.
+        ID3D12PipelineState* TryGetForUse(COMMAND_LIST_TYPE CommandListType)
+        {
+            if (!m_bReady.load(std::memory_order_acquire))
+            {
+                return nullptr;
+            }
+            return GetForUse(CommandListType);
+        }
+
     protected:
         const EPipelineType m_PipelineStateType;
         RootSignature* const m_pRootSignature;
@@ -154,6 +167,12 @@ namespace D3D12TranslationLayer
         UINT SOStrides[D3D12_SO_STREAM_COUNT];
 
         CThreadPoolWork m_ThreadpoolWork;
+        // Set once CreateImpl has returned or thrown, on whichever thread ran it.
+        std::atomic<bool> m_bReady{ false };
+
+        // Out of line: it reports the wait to the ImmediateContext, which is
+        // incomplete where this header is included.
+        void WaitForCreate();
 
         template<EPipelineType Type>
         void Create();
diff --git a/src/PipelineState.cpp b/src/PipelineState.cpp
index df977f7..accfd84 100644
--- a/src/PipelineState.cpp
+++ b/src/PipelineState.cpp
@@ -95,14 +95,25 @@ namespace D3D12TranslationLayer
                     CreateImpl<Type>();
                 }
                 catch (RelayHResultError&) {}
+                m_bReady.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
             });
         }
         else
         {
             CreateImpl<Type>();
+            m_bReady.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
         }
     }
 
+    void PipelineState::WaitForCreate()
+    {
+        LARGE_INTEGER Start, End;
+        QueryPerformanceCounter(&Start);
+        m_ThreadpoolWork.Wait(false);
+        QueryPerformanceCounter(&End);
+        m_pParent->RecordPSOWait(End.QuadPart - Start.QuadPart);
+    }
+
     template<EPipelineType Type>
     inline void PipelineState::CreateImpl()
     {
